1
00:00:00,100 --> 00:00:05,120
You step onto a padel court with fifteen years
of tennis experience and a heavy

2
00:00:05,120 --> 00:00:05,497
serve.

3
00:00:05,847 --> 00:00:11,223
Ten minutes in, you are losing to two
recreational players who barely look athletic.

4
00:00:11,573 --> 00:00:16,912
Every time you crush a forehand, they smile
and tap an easy winner into an open

5
00:00:16,912 --> 00:00:17,312
court.

6
00:00:17,662 --> 00:00:21,161
Your tennis instincts are actively
sabotaging your game.

7
00:00:21,511 --> 00:00:25,721
Today, I will show you the five tennis
habits killing your progress,

8
00:00:25,721 --> 00:00:28,466
the physics behind them, and
how to fix them.

9
00:00:28,815 --> 00:00:32,684
Padel looks like tennis in a glass
box, but tactically,

10
00:00:32,684 --> 00:00:34,895
it is almost the exact opposite.

11
00:00:35,245 --> 00:00:38,850
In tennis, hitting hard into open
court ends the point.

12
00:00:39,201 --> 00:00:44,001
In padel, hitting hard against the glass
feeds your opponent an easy counter.

13
00:00:44,351 --> 00:00:46,448
In tennis, the baseline is home.

14
00:00:46,448 --> 00:00:50,324
In padel, camping back there is a
statistical death sentence.

15
00:00:50,674 --> 00:00:55,434
To unlock your skills, you must unlearn
five habits: the power trap,

16
00:00:55,434 --> 00:01:01,021
the lob misunderstanding, baseline camping,
wall panic, and large looping swings.

17
00:01:01,371 --> 00:01:06,704
Master these five shifts, and your tennis
background becomes an unfair advantage.

18
00:01:07,054 --> 00:01:12,259
In tennis, hitting hard and deep wins points
because the court ends at the baseline.

19
00:01:12,609 --> 00:01:16,321
In padel, the court ends in
10-millimeter tempered glass.

20
00:01:16,671 --> 00:01:22,474
Tempered glass returns up to 70 percent of
incoming ball speed back into the court.

21
00:01:22,824 --> 00:01:28,345
When you blast a flat drive or smash, the ball
hits the turf, slams the back glass,

22
00:01:28,345 --> 00:01:30,909
and rebounds waist-high into the court.

23
00:01:31,259 --> 00:01:34,331
You served an easy sitter to two
waiting opponents.

24
00:01:34,681 --> 00:01:39,909
Topspin makes it worse: it grips the vertical
glass and kicks upward into an easy

25
00:01:39,909 --> 00:01:40,228
kill.

26
00:01:40,578 --> 00:01:45,045
Crushing the ball into the glass is like
throwing a rubber ball at a brick

27
00:01:45,045 --> 00:01:47,725
fireplace; it ricochets
straight back at you.

28
00:01:48,075 --> 00:01:53,977
In one study of pro finals, smashes made up
only 12 percent of attacking shots—and

29
00:01:53,977 --> 00:01:57,035
flat smashes were only a
fraction of those.

30
00:01:57,385 --> 00:02:01,888
Volleys account for roughly 65
percent of attacking shots,

31
00:02:01,888 --> 00:02:04,788
and slice bandejas make up 23 percent.

32
00:02:05,137 --> 00:02:11,349
The fix is the low-rebound rule: keep
groundstrokes at 60 to 70 percent pace with

33
00:02:11,349 --> 00:02:12,561
heavy underspin.

34
00:02:12,911 --> 00:02:16,474
Slice bites the glass and dies
downward onto the turf.

35
00:02:16,824 --> 00:02:22,611
Train the Glass Rebound Gauge drill: hit
baseline slice drives so the glass rebound

36
00:02:22,611 --> 00:02:25,229
bounces twice before the service line.

37
00:02:25,579 --> 00:02:29,739
Do 4 sets of 10 reps on each
side, resting 60 seconds.

38
00:02:30,089 --> 00:02:34,078
In tennis, the lob is a defensive
bail-out when stretched wide.

39
00:02:34,429 --> 00:02:39,378
In padel, the lob is the single most
important offensive weapon in the sport.

40
00:02:39,728 --> 00:02:45,584
Match data shows players choose the lob in over
60 percent of successful transitions

41
00:02:45,584 --> 00:02:47,237
from defense to offense.

42
00:02:47,587 --> 00:02:52,366
A padel court is only 10 meters wide,
guarded by two net players.

43
00:02:52,716 --> 00:02:56,469
Blasting passing shots gives them
easy reflex volleys,

44
00:02:56,469 --> 00:02:59,607
and missed balls rebound off
the glass anyway.

45
00:02:59,957 --> 00:03:02,605
A high lob stays airborne for 3 seconds,

46
00:03:02,605 --> 00:03:07,061
giving you and your partner time to
sprint forward and steal the net.

47
00:03:07,411 --> 00:03:12,994
A padel lob is like castling in chess: it evicts
opponents from the high ground and

48
00:03:12,994 --> 00:03:14,323
flips court control.

49
00:03:14,673 --> 00:03:17,536
The fix is the high-arc baseline eviction.

50
00:03:17,536 --> 00:03:21,065
Bend your knees, tilt the paddle
face up 20 degrees,

51
00:03:21,065 --> 00:03:25,660
and lift with your legs and shoulder
rather than flicking your wrist.

52
00:03:26,009 --> 00:03:29,358
Aim deep, between the service
line and the back glass.

53
00:03:29,709 --> 00:03:35,377
Practice the Lob Target Box drill: mark a
2-meter box in the back corner and hit

54
00:03:35,377 --> 00:03:37,197
high lobs off fed volleys.

55
00:03:37,547 --> 00:03:41,280
Do 4 sets of 12 reps, resting 45 seconds.

56
00:03:41,630 --> 00:03:44,602
Then run the Lob and Charge
drill: lob deep,

57
00:03:44,602 --> 00:03:47,442
and the instant it clears the net players,

58
00:03:47,442 --> 00:03:52,659
call your lanes and sprint forward to lock in
at the 3-meter net line together.

59
00:03:53,009 --> 00:03:56,629
Modern tennis is dominated by
baseline rallies,

60
00:03:56,629 --> 00:04:02,737
with players contesting over 75 to 80 percent
of points from behind the baseline.

61
00:04:03,087 --> 00:04:06,116
In padel, staying back
destroys your win rate.

62
00:04:06,467 --> 00:04:12,213
Research shows over 80 percent of all points in
padel are won by the team occupying

63
00:04:12,213 --> 00:04:12,760
the net.

64
00:04:13,110 --> 00:04:16,314
Winning pairs attack in 85
percent of points,

65
00:04:16,314 --> 00:04:19,169
while losing pairs attack in barely half.

66
00:04:19,519 --> 00:04:24,490
Staying back surrenders 70 percent of the
court geometry to your opponents.

67
00:04:24,839 --> 00:04:28,951
Worse, if one partner rushes forward
while the other camps back,

68
00:04:28,951 --> 00:04:32,050
you open a huge diagonal
channel down the middle.

69
00:04:32,400 --> 00:04:37,805
Camping on the baseline is like packing all
eleven soccer players inside your own

70
00:04:37,805 --> 00:04:40,507
penalty box; you cannot score from there.

71
00:04:40,857 --> 00:04:45,107
The fix is the 3-meter net lock:
position yourself 2.

72
00:04:45,107 --> 00:04:47,705
5 to 3 meters behind the net cord.

73
00:04:48,055 --> 00:04:53,083
This sweet spot lets you intercept volleys
above net level while leaving room to

74
00:04:53,083 --> 00:04:54,263
backpedal for lobs.

75
00:04:54,613 --> 00:05:00,117
Train the Invisible Rope drill: connect
yourselves with an imaginary 3-meter cord

76
00:05:00,117 --> 00:05:04,682
during shadow footwork or mirror rallies
without physical tethering.

77
00:05:05,032 --> 00:05:09,768
When one moves forward, both move forward;
when one retreats, both retreat.

78
00:05:10,118 --> 00:05:15,025
Do 3 sets of 5-minute continuous
rallies, resting 90 seconds.

79
00:05:15,375 --> 00:05:19,002
In tennis, if the ball gets behind
you, the point is over.

80
00:05:19,351 --> 00:05:22,569
When a fast ball travels deep
toward the corners,

81
00:05:22,569 --> 00:05:27,074
tennis players panic and try awkward
half-volleys off their shoelaces.

82
00:05:27,424 --> 00:05:30,624
In padel, the back glass is
your ultimate ally.

83
00:05:30,974 --> 00:05:36,246
When a fast ball passes you, letting it
strike the turf and glass absorbs its

84
00:05:36,246 --> 00:05:37,395
forward momentum.

85
00:05:37,745 --> 00:05:42,886
The ball rebounds forward into your strike
zone at a slower, manageable speed.

86
00:05:43,237 --> 00:05:47,952
By the law of reflection, the angle of
entry matches the angle of exit.

87
00:05:48,301 --> 00:05:52,818
Tennis players get trapped because they face
the net and backpedal straight back,

88
00:05:52,818 --> 00:05:55,021
sandwiching themselves against the wall.

89
00:05:55,371 --> 00:06:00,445
Fighting the glass is like trying to jump
through a revolving door at full sprint.

90
00:06:00,445 --> 00:06:03,563
Step aside, let it turn, and
walk through smoothly.

91
00:06:03,913 --> 00:06:05,959
The fix is to open the door.

92
00:06:05,959 --> 00:06:09,205
The moment the ball crosses
the service line,

93
00:06:09,205 --> 00:06:12,169
rotate your shoulders 90 degrees sideways.

94
00:06:12,519 --> 00:06:15,594
Let the ball pass your hips,
bounce off the glass,

95
00:06:15,594 --> 00:06:18,428
and strike it on its forward
path out in front.

96
00:06:18,779 --> 00:06:22,255
Train the Catch and Hit Glass
drill: without a racket,

97
00:06:22,255 --> 00:06:25,542
have a partner feed deep balls
into the back corner.

98
00:06:25,891 --> 00:06:29,904
Turn sideways, let the ball bounce on
the turf, strike the glass,

99
00:06:29,904 --> 00:06:31,971
and catch it in front of your hip.

100
00:06:32,321 --> 00:06:35,154
Do 2 sets of 10 catches on each side,

101
00:06:35,154 --> 00:06:38,956
then hit 4 sets of 12 slice
drives off the rebound.

102
00:06:39,306 --> 00:06:42,651
This is the most dangerous mistake
for a tennis player,

103
00:06:42,651 --> 00:06:44,682
both for your score and your body.

104
00:06:45,032 --> 00:06:50,643
Tennis players use huge, looping backswings with
Western grips to generate topspin.

105
00:06:50,993 --> 00:06:55,665
Padel points average 10 to 15
seconds with rapid exchanges.

106
00:06:56,015 --> 00:07:01,180
A big backswing means your racket is still
traveling backward when the ball arrives,

107
00:07:01,180 --> 00:07:03,610
forcing late contact and wrist flicking.

108
00:07:03,959 --> 00:07:09,868
A padel racket is a solid composite plate
with no strings to absorb vibration.

109
00:07:10,219 --> 00:07:15,495
Striking off-center with a loose wrist sends
harsh impact shocks straight into your

110
00:07:15,495 --> 00:07:17,003
forearm extensor tendon.

111
00:07:17,353 --> 00:07:20,376
Lateral epicondylitis, or padel elbow,

112
00:07:20,376 --> 00:07:24,329
accounts for over 20 percent of
all padel injuries.

113
00:07:24,679 --> 00:07:29,767
And when tennis players jump for high balls
with a tennis service motion,

114
00:07:29,767 --> 00:07:33,961
violent internal shoulder rotation
pinches the rotator cuff,

115
00:07:33,961 --> 00:07:36,092
causing 15 percent of injuries.

116
00:07:36,442 --> 00:07:41,970
Playing padel with a tennis swing is like
driving an 18-wheel truck through an

117
00:07:41,970 --> 00:07:45,679
indoor go-kart track; the turning
radius is too wide.

118
00:07:46,029 --> 00:07:50,296
The fix has two parts: the compact
punch volley and the bandeja.

119
00:07:50,646 --> 00:07:54,571
Use a continental hammer grip for 80
percent of your shots.

120
00:07:54,921 --> 00:07:59,672
On volleys, never let the racket head
travel behind your lead shoulder.

121
00:07:59,672 --> 00:08:03,433
Turn your chest, step forward, and
punch down with slice.

122
00:08:03,783 --> 00:08:07,474
On overheads, replace the flat
smash with the bandeja.

123
00:08:07,824 --> 00:08:11,664
Set your racket up like a tray at ear
height with an open face.

124
00:08:12,014 --> 00:08:16,899
Slice across the bottom of the ball and finish
wrapping your racket around your neck

125
00:08:16,899 --> 00:08:17,646
like a scarf.

126
00:08:17,996 --> 00:08:23,585
The bandeja keeps your elbow bent, drastically
reduces shoulder impingement stress,

127
00:08:23,585 --> 00:08:26,380
and keeps the ball low off the back glass.

128
00:08:26,730 --> 00:08:32,386
Practice the Wall Behind the Back drill: stand
30 to 40 centimeters in front of the

129
00:08:32,386 --> 00:08:36,022
wall and start with shadow swings
or soft hand feeds.

130
00:08:36,022 --> 00:08:39,658
If your racket clips the wall on
your takeback, reset.

131
00:08:40,008 --> 00:08:43,229
Progress to 4 sets of 15 compact volleys.

132
00:08:43,579 --> 00:08:49,269
If you ever feel burning pain in your outer elbow
or sharp catching in your shoulder,

133
00:08:49,269 --> 00:08:52,048
stop and consult a sports physiotherapist.

134
00:08:52,399 --> 00:08:57,263
Here is how to reprogram your tennis muscle
memory over the next 4 weeks.

135
00:08:57,613 --> 00:09:02,716
In week 1, eliminate the flat power
smash, cap your overhead volume,

136
00:09:02,716 --> 00:09:07,597
and play all overheads as controlled
bandejas at 60 percent speed.

137
00:09:07,947 --> 00:09:13,759
In week 2, master the lob: hit at least 5 deep
lobs per set to push opponents off

138
00:09:13,759 --> 00:09:14,326
the net.

139
00:09:14,675 --> 00:09:19,944
In week 3, implement the 3-meter net rule and
tandem movement with your partner.

140
00:09:20,295 --> 00:09:25,673
In week 4, drill the Catch and Hit off the
back glass until wall rebounds feel

141
00:09:25,673 --> 00:09:26,354
automatic.

142
00:09:26,703 --> 00:09:32,323
To protect your elbow, use a round racket with
a soft foam core and add an extra

143
00:09:32,323 --> 00:09:34,682
overgrip to reduce forearm strain.

144
00:09:35,032 --> 00:09:39,555
Padel is not mini-tennis; it is
tactical chess on a glass board.

145
00:09:39,905 --> 00:09:44,769
Stop fighting the glass, stop smashing from
deep, and start owning the net.

146
00:09:45,119 --> 00:09:50,236
The next time you walk onto the court, your
tennis skills will finally work for you,

147
00:09:50,236 --> 00:09:51,199
not against you.

148
00:09:51,549 --> 00:09:54,728
All sources are cited in the
description below.
